===============================================================================
PROJECT CONTEXT AND INTENT
===============================================================================

tabgha is one component of a larger project that gathers liturgical texts from a
wide range of languages and copyright holders. Working directly on the official
texts is essential to that work, so the example/reference files above are kept
deliberately rather than replaced with substitutes.

When the larger project is published, the CODE (which we own and license) will be
kept separate from the COLLECTED DATA (texts copied from others), so that it is
always clear what is authored by us and what is reproduced from third parties,
each under its own copyright and permissions.

Until then, this notice records that distinction.
